 "takes": [
  {
   "take": 0,
   "beat": "hook",
   "text": "In 1940, a brand-new bridge in Washington State started to dance.",
   "t0": 0.298,
   "t1": 4.448,
   "pause_after": 0.25
  },
  {
   "take": 1,
   "beat": "hook",
   "text": "Locals called it Galloping Gertie, and people drove across just to feel it bounce.",
   "t0": 4.8505,
   "t1": 9.1255,
   "pause_after": 0.35
  },
  {
   "take": 2,
   "beat": "ribbon",
   "text": "Its main span was over half a mile long, but its deck was only eight feet deep.",
   "t0": 9.6105,
   "t1": 13.8355,
   "pause_after": 0.2
  },
  {
   "take": 3,
   "beat": "ribbon",
   "text": "In the wind, it rippled like a ribbon.",
   "t0": 14.1919,
   "t1": 16.0919,
   "pause_after": 0.35
  },
  {
   "take": 4,
   "beat": "wind",
   "text": "On November seventh, four months after it opened, a steady wind of about forty miles an hour began to blow.",
   "t0": 16.577,
   "t1": 22.702,
   "pause_after": 0.3
  },
  {
   "take": 5,
   "beat": "twist",
   "text": "Then the motion changed. The bounce turned into a twist.",
   "t0": 23.1531,
   "t1": 26.1031,
   "pause_after": 0.2
  },
  {
   "take": 6,
   "beat": "twist",
   "text": "As the deck tilted, the wind caught it at an angle and pushed it further.",
   "t0": 26.45,
   "t1": 30.175,
   "pause_after": 0.2
  },
  {
   "take": 7,
   "beat": "twist",
   "text": "Every twist fed the next one. The wind was pumping energy in faster than the bridge could lose it.",
   "t0": 30.5279,
   "t1": 35.9279,
   "pause_after": 0.35
  },
  {
   "take": 8,
   "beat": "film",
   "text": "This is real film from that morning.",
   "t0": 36.4275,
   "t1": 38.2275,
   "pause_after": 0.3
  },
  {
   "take": 9,
   "beat": "tubby",
   "text": "One man fled his car on the bridge, with his daughter's dog, Tubby, still inside.",
   "t0": 38.6785,
   "t1": 42.9035,
   "pause_after": 0.35
  },
  {
   "take": 10,
   "beat": "fall",
   "text": "Around eleven, the deck tore loose and fell into the water.",
   "t0": 43.4042,
   "t1": 46.5042,
   "pause_after": 0.45
  },
  {
   "take": 11,
   "beat": "myth",
   "text": "For decades, textbooks blamed resonance, the wind matching the bridge's rhythm.",
   "t0": 47.1115,
   "t1": 51.4115,
   "pause_after": 0.2
  },
  {
   "take": 12,
   "beat": "myth",
   "text": "It wasn't. The bridge made its own rhythm, and the wind kept feeding it.",
   "t0": 51.7465,
   "t1": 55.5215,
   "pause_after": 0.35
  },
  {
   "take": 13,
   "beat": "lesson",
   "text": "That's why big bridges are now tested in wind tunnels before they're built.",
   "t0": 56.017,
   "t1": 59.867,
   "pause_after": 0.2
  },
  {
   "take": 14,
   "beat": "lesson",
   "text": "So they never learn to dance.",
   "t0": 60.2658,
   "t1": 61.7408,
   "pause_after": 0.7
  }
 ]
}